1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,491
The Features page is where you choose what your Orchard Core site runs.

2
00:00:05,491 --> 00:00:09,690
In this video, you find it, search and filter its list, and enable

3
00:00:09,690 --> 00:00:13,190
and disable features one at a time or several at once.

4
00:00:17,790 --> 00:00:20,830
Orchard Core is divided into modules.

5
00:00:20,830 --> 00:00:26,980
Each module provides one or more features, such as Media, Workflows, or Sitemaps.

6
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:31,586
Your site runs only the features that are enabled, and the recipe you

7
00:00:31,586 --> 00:00:34,620
choose at setup decides which ones start out enabled.

8
00:00:35,370 --> 00:00:40,548
An enabled feature can add admin menu entries, settings pages, and permissions.

9
00:00:40,548 --> 00:00:44,812
A feature that is disabled adds none of them, so the admin shows

10
00:00:44,812 --> 00:00:46,700
only what your site uses.

11
00:00:47,450 --> 00:00:49,701
Features can depend on one another.

12
00:00:49,701 --> 00:00:54,314
Enabling a feature also enables the features it needs, and disabling a feature

13
00:00:54,314 --> 00:00:56,840
also disables the features that need it.

14
00:00:56,840 --> 00:00:59,860
A separate video explains dependencies in detail.

15
00:01:04,108 --> 00:01:06,162
Let's open the Features page.

16
00:01:06,162 --> 00:01:09,508
In the admin menu, open Tools, and choose Features.

17
00:01:11,794 --> 00:01:16,049
The page lists the features in groups, one group for each category.

18
00:01:16,049 --> 00:01:19,954
Above the list, a summary shows how many features are listed.

19
00:01:20,416 --> 00:01:24,618
Each row shows the name of a feature, with its identifier beside it.

20
00:01:24,618 --> 00:01:28,763
Badges show the features it depends on and whether it is Enabled or

21
00:01:28,763 --> 00:01:31,716
Disabled, and the description sits underneath.

22
00:01:32,167 --> 00:01:35,817
A button at the end of a row changes the state of that feature.

23
00:01:35,817 --> 00:01:39,414
Enable turns on a feature that is off, and Disable turns off a

24
00:01:39,414 --> 00:01:40,737
feature that is on.

25
00:01:45,029 --> 00:01:48,070
The search box narrows the list as you type.

26
00:01:48,070 --> 00:01:51,355
It matches names, identifiers, and descriptions.

27
00:01:51,355 --> 00:01:53,789
Let's search for background tasks.

28
00:01:54,273 --> 00:01:57,187
One row is left, and the summary counts it.

29
00:01:57,187 --> 00:02:00,993
Press Escape to clear the search, and the list comes back.

30
00:02:01,456 --> 00:02:05,140
The Status filter limits the list to features that are enabled, or to

31
00:02:05,140 --> 00:02:06,614
those that are disabled.

32
00:02:06,614 --> 00:02:09,856
Choose Enabled only to list the features that are turned on.

33
00:02:10,322 --> 00:02:14,210
The Visibility filter hides two kinds of features by default.

34
00:02:14,210 --> 00:02:19,491
Hide on demand covers features that are enabled only when another feature needs them.

35
00:02:19,491 --> 00:02:24,772
Hide always enabled covers features that are always enabled and cannot be turned off.

36
00:02:25,234 --> 00:02:27,448
Let's clear Hide always enabled.

37
00:02:27,448 --> 00:02:32,692
Features, the feature behind this page, joins the list with a dimmed Disable button.

38
00:02:32,692 --> 00:02:37,644
Pointing at it shows that it is always enabled and cannot be manually disabled.

39
00:02:41,864 --> 00:02:43,951
Let's enable Background Tasks.

40
00:02:43,951 --> 00:02:48,414
Search for it, and its row shows a Disabled badge and an Enable button.

41
00:02:48,875 --> 00:02:49,927
Click Enable.

42
00:02:49,927 --> 00:02:54,135
The page reloads, and a message confirms that the feature was enabled.

43
00:02:54,593 --> 00:02:59,308
Under Tools in the admin menu, a Background Tasks entry appears.

44
00:02:59,308 --> 00:03:04,023
In the list, the row shows Enabled, and its button says Disable.

45
00:03:08,323 --> 00:03:10,358
Let's disable Background Tasks.

46
00:03:10,358 --> 00:03:13,053
Search for it and click Disable on its row.

47
00:03:13,505 --> 00:03:17,104
A dialog titled Disable Feature asks you to confirm.

48
00:03:17,104 --> 00:03:20,515
Click Yes to continue, or No to keep the feature.

49
00:03:21,009 --> 00:03:22,143
Let's click Yes.

50
00:03:22,143 --> 00:03:26,061
The page reloads with a message that the feature was disabled, and the

51
00:03:26,061 --> 00:03:28,999
Background Tasks entry is gone from the Tools menu.

52
00:03:33,210 --> 00:03:37,299
To change several features together, use the checkbox on each row.

53
00:03:37,299 --> 00:03:41,900
Let's search for google, and check Google Analytics and Google Tag Manager.

54
00:03:45,011 --> 00:03:46,406
Open Bulk Actions.

55
00:03:46,406 --> 00:03:50,532
Disable turns the checked features off, and Enable turns them on.

56
00:03:50,532 --> 00:03:53,961
Neither asks for confirmation, so let's click Enable.

57
00:03:54,415 --> 00:03:57,861
The page reloads with a message naming both features.

58
00:03:57,861 --> 00:04:03,350
Searching for google again shows them as Enabled, while Google Authentication, which was

59
00:04:03,350 --> 00:04:05,335
not checked, stays Disabled.

60
00:04:09,535 --> 00:04:14,092
Only users with the Manage Features permission can open the Features page.

61
00:04:14,092 --> 00:04:16,769
The Administrator role has it by default.

62
00:04:16,769 --> 00:04:21,155
To give it to another role, edit that role under Access Control, Roles.

63
00:04:23,155 --> 00:04:27,866
The Features page, under Tools, lets you enable and disable the features your

64
00:04:27,866 --> 00:04:30,250
site runs, one at a time or in bulk.

65
00:04:30,250 --> 00:04:31,725
Thanks for watching.

